    "id": "110ad19aab36548b6fa20b84fcbbdd6556839556",
    "message": "fix(eap): reject disguised remote HTTP targets before using credentials\n\nA loopback-looking string prefix accepted userinfo URLs whose actual HTTP host was remote. Parse and validate scheme, hostname and port; reject userinfo and raw whitespace/control characters before configuring the authenticated client. Keep the existing redirect and observation-bound receipt guards.\n\nSeven constructor-negative cases reproduce false acceptance on the unchanged predecessor. The repair passes 162 targeted tests and the complete local make test (2285 reported Python executions). Preserve full raw logs as verified gzip files and deterministically generated integrity (5395 entries / 5384 digests). The final evidence/metadata-only delta and exact remote-head native CI remain explicitly separate.\n\nExtend only the existing isolated carrier from 1c314c0004032fa819392f82a5184f6acc79ff87. Concurrent PR546 was reobserved at 9fe7057167beb381c3f3272c6e6d2b977529113d/tree e56b962fe9a5ba623f06ae89235e6f7ca1a852b5 and remains untouched. Reconciliation, seven-checker/native/governance acceptance and Main integration are open.\n\nOriginal Claude contribution and Codex repairs remain attributed. No Mirror runtime adoption, live EAP send, host token grant, deployment or productive EFFECT_ACK_DONE is claimed.",
    "timestamp": "2026-10-31T20:56:56Z",
    "tree_id": "970d497294bc3595bbede81d40bcced8e40f7d60"
  },
